You are now arguing with the tarmi definition, not me:

[also pattern; x1 is the mathematical or theoretical ideal form,
while x2 is an object/event manifesting that form; e.g.
circular/circle-shaped (= cukseltai) vs. circle (=cuktai, while
cukla alone is ambiguous);

Also, from cukla:

[normally used for a filled-in circle/disk, but
emphasis on roundness means that the concept may
include 'ring'];

So at the least you should probably be using djine if you insist on
avoiding cuktai.

